module

public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.ToLin

/-!
# Integer certificates for the F4 torus stabilizer calculation

These are candidate matrices and short simple words for the actual F4 Weyl
action in fundamental weight coordinates. Ordinary paths record root
reflections and doubled-displacement witnesses. Sixteen exceptional elements
are conjugates of one representative; its four cubic-torsion kernel cases
have their own reflection paths and displacement-plus-line witnesses.

The definitions alone assert no coverage or factorization theorem. The
separate kernel checks and native Weyl-action comparison certify them before
they enter the actual torus-centralizer consumer. The table generation uses
exact integer arithmetic; its output, not its Python generator, is checked.

Source: Steinberg, GLS3 Chapter 2, 8.2(6)–(7) and 8.3(c), on the full F4
weight lattice. The determinant-nine cases retain the genuine cubic torsion.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

namespace Theory.AlgebraicGroup.StandardRootSystem.F4WeightAction.Stabilizer.Data

